  "tail_text": "dijkstra` so non-negative edges yield the true shortest distance.\n\nunicaa01_p21_panic/main.py\n```python\n\"\"\"Dijkstra shortest paths for non-negative weights.\"\"\"\nfrom heapq import heappop, heappush\n\n\ndef dijkstra(adj, src):\n    dist = {src: 0}\n    pq = [(0, src)]\n    seen = set()\n    while pq:\n        d, u = heappop(pq)\n        if u in seen:\n            continue\n        seen.add(u)\n        for v, w in adj.get(u, []):\n            nd = d + w\n            if v not in dist or nd < dist[v]:\n                dist[v] = nd\n                heappush(pq, (nd, v))\n    return dist\n\n\ndef demo():\n    adj = {0: [(1, 1), (2, 5)], 1: [(2, 3)], 2: []}\n    return dijkstra(adj, 0)[2]\n```",
  "full_completion_text": "dijkstra` so non-negative edges yield the true shortest distance.\n\nunicaa01_p21_panic/main.py\n```python\n\"\"\"Dijkstra shortest paths for non-negative weights.\"\"\"\nfrom heapq import heappop, heappush\n\n\ndef dijkstra(adj, src):\n    dist = {src: 0}\n    pq = [(0, src)]\n    seen = set()\n    while pq:\n        d, u = heappop(pq)\n        if u in seen:\n            continue\n        seen.add(u)\n        for v, w in adj.get(u, []):\n            nd = d + w\n            if v not in dist or nd < dist[v]:\n                dist[v] = nd\n                heappush(pq, (nd, v))\n    return dist\n\n\ndef demo():\n    adj = {0: [(1, 1), (2, 5)], 1: [(2, 3)], 2: []}\n    return dijkstra(adj, 0)[2]\n```",
